-- title:
--   j=0 is preserved by Vélu quotients in characteristic 2 or 3
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field with decidable equality whose characteristic is $2$ or $3$ (i.e. `ringChar K = 2 ∨ ringChar K = 3`), let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $K$ that is elliptic (its discriminant is a unit) with $j(W)=0$. Let $Q$ be a point of the affine curve attached to $W$ with $\operatorname{addOrderOf} Q = N$, and form the Vélu-type quotient `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N`: the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1,a_2,a_3$ as $W$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4-5t$ and $a_6$ by $a_6-b_2t-7w$, where $t=\sum (3x^2+2a_2x+a_4-a_1y)$ and $w=\sum\bigl(x(3x^2+2a_2x+a_4-a_1y)+y(2y+a_1x+a_3)\bigr)$, both sums taken over the finite set of pairs $(x,y)\in K\times K$ obtained as the coordinates (or the default value at the point at infinity) of $k\cdot Q$ for $1\le k\le N-1$. Assuming the discriminant $\Delta$ of this quotient curve is nonzero, so that the quotient is itself elliptic, the conclusion is that its $j$-invariant is also $0$.
--
--   In characteristic $2$ and $3$ the condition $j=0$ cuts out the supersingular locus, and the statement records that this condition passes to the Vélu quotient by the subgroup generated by a point; no primality of $N$ and no extension of $K$ are needed. It is used in the study of the $j$-line on modular curves, by [`ModularCurve.evalAt_jNGeomGen_eq_zero_of_mem_ssPlaces_of_lt_five`](thm.html#ModularCurve.evalAt_jNGeomGen_eq_zero_of_mem_ssPlaces_of_lt_five) and [`ModularCurve.placeRamificationJ_mul_jWidth_evalAt_jNGeomGen_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.placeRamificationJ_mul_jWidth_evalAt_jNGeomGen_eq).
